kq gains view_allocs and view_frees, two counters the runtime did not have
before, so its cost goldens grow two lines. They cannot be regenerated on kq
first: kq pins a kanso sha and its pinned compiler does not emit them, so the
numbers do not exist until this lands.

What moves: two counter lines appear, nothing else. No existing counter changes
value — verified against every kanso cost golden and mem file, all of which show
the same two additions and no other movement.

What got better in exchange: a leak that was invisible becomes a diffed fact.
The map view cache had no counter at all, so 76,800,048 bytes over 1.6 million
iterations could not be seen by anything CI runs. It is now two numbers whose
gap CI watches.
